s of delivering a valuable product to end users, but they differ in focus and timing. QA is a proactive process that starts with defining procedures, rules, and policies for selecting and using raw materials in the manufacturing process. It is focused on managing the process to ensure that business goals are met within a set period of time. On the other hand, QC is focused on the evaluation process and takes place during and after the manufacturing process. It is product-oriented and is aimed at ensuring the quality of the finished product.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}", "role": "user"}], "model": "unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF", "seed": 69410, "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1}
