or and season it as desired. Place the seasoned meat in an uncovered roasting pan on a shelf in the bottom third of your oven. Bake exactly for 5 and a half minutes per pound. Adjust the time more or less according to your oven's accuracy and heat retention. After cooking, remove the pork from the oven, lightly cover it with foil and let it rest for 5-10 minutes to allow the internal juices to redistribute. The roast should be very slightly pink in the center and very moist. After resting for 10 minutes, the roast should reach a safe temperature of 145-150 degrees.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}", "role": "user"}], "model": "unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF", "seed": 69410, "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1}
