":\\\"Padaro Beach Grill\\\",\\\"review_info\\\":[{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2022-01-18 03:32:06\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":4.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"I give the food here 5/5 very delicious I've had their burgers and sandwiches. Their sweet potato fries are really good. In my opinion the food is pricey but if your hungry and don't mind spending a bit more by all means yes. But well their service there is sometimes great sometime not so great just depends who takes your order. But the food and view are great.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-12-08 05:09:40\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":5.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"What's a surprising treat. We were road-tripping and wanted to grab some fresh affordable fish and ended up at Padrino's. Their fresh fish was perfectly matched by the ambiance as you could sit outside close to the ocean. Casual, good quality, and beautiful! Highly recommend!\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-11-29 17:17:46\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":5.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"What an adorable place!!! Loved the Ambience, the beautiful outside seating, the cozy and warm fire pits and the delicious food! I got the Turkey burger with caramelized onions and avocados, OMG!! My taste buds were bursting with joy!! Love it and can't wait to go back on a warmer day!!\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"original_answer\": \"Bring the salmon to room temperature 10 minutes before cooking. Warm a large non-stick skillet with oil over medium-low heat. Season the salmon with salt and pepper, then raise the heat to medium-high. Place the salmon skin-side down on the pan. Let it cook undisturbed for 2 minutes if it's a thin fillet, up to 4 minutes if it's a thick 2-inch fillet. Do not move the fillets. After the initial cooking period, turn the fillets and cook about 3 minutes more, or until it feels firm to the touch and is just barely pink in the center. The skin can be served or easily removed with a knife or spoon. Serve immediately.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in