irstly tackle difficult food stains by soaking the pan in warm water, without soap, for 15 minutes to loosen stuck-on food particles. After removing the pan from the water, pour 1 tsp. of mild hand dish-washing detergent into your kitchen sink and fill it with hot water. Place your Le Creuset grill pan in this soapy solution and scrub gently with a nylon dish scrubber. Then, rinse the grill pan with plain, warm water to get rid of the soapy solution. Finally, hand dry your Le Creuset cast iron grill pan with a dish towel to prevent rust.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}", "role": "user"}], "model": "unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF", "seed": 69410, "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1}
