ew_text\\\":\\\"I love this place so much, but I am heartbroken to say that they closed as of March 3rd. I am just happy I got to go there the Friday before that, without knowing it would be my last visit. I'll miss you Sunnyside!\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2013-06-04 23:37:56\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":3.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"While waiting for your food, you can look around and shop for $900 microwave ovens, $800 mixers and even a $10,000 convection steamer oven! \\\\n\\\\nWait, there's more! On the other side with the chips and drinks you can find nail clippers and combs! I didn't ask what they had behind the counter but I bet they had some questionable items for sale back there, hidden from view.\\\\n\\\\nNow, as far as the food. Pastrami was good with a lot of it. Bread was stale and fell apart...bummer.\\\\n\\\\nChicken bacon panini, believe it or not, had too much bacon. \\\\n\\\\nFood is 2 1/2 star. Prices are on the \\\\\\\"low\\\\\\\" side for Santa Barbara @ $7.95 for a big sandwich. So, half extra star for that.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2013-04-30 23:21:15\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":1.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Dont go!  just got back from there and bit into my cold cut sandwhich and it was horrible.  The bread was dry the spirinkling of bitter iceburg lettuce and soggy tomato just made everything worse.  There is no love in the food at this place.  How do places so bad stay open.  I would never go back if someone even offered to buy me lunch.  my stomach is ont very happy!\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"original_answer\": \"Two connected shootings occurred in Washington on Thursday, one at the U.S. Census Bureau's headquarters and another in a busy restaurant area. The incidents began with a suspected domestic kidnapping. A guard was critically injured at the Census Bureau after approaching a vehicle in which two people were arguing. Following a police chase and shootout, an officer and the suspect were wounded. The kidnap victim was found i